error[E0439]: an actor's message can't take a `mut` parameter: messages carry values
  --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/not_here.la:6:34
  |
6 | actor A { x: i64, fun take(self, mut n: i64) {} }
  |                                  ^^^
  |
  = help: an actor is started with `spawn` and reached only through its methods; what crosses its boundary is copied and may hold no `Ref`

error[E0438]: `spawn` of a call that changes its receiver or a `mut` argument: the new thread would change its own copy
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/not_here.la:14:19
   |
14 |     let t = spawn bump(mut x);
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: nobody would see the change; send the new value back through a channel, or keep it in a `Ref`

error[E0406]: `bump` can't be used as a value
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/not_here.la:15:13
   |
15 |     let f = bump;
   |             ^^^^
   |
   = help: a function with a `mut` parameter can't be a value: wrap the call in a closure that returns the changed value

error[E0422]: `impl Grow for G` doesn't match `Grow`
   --> tests/programs/functions/mut_params/not_here.la:10:6
   |
10 | impl Grow for G { fun grow(self, n: i64) {} }
   |      ^^^^
   |
   = help: `grow` should be `fun grow(self, mut i64)`

For more about E0439, E0438, E0406 and E0422, run `lughac explain <code>`.
